{"path":"\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/' data-target='root' data-title=''>&#8962; <\/a>\r\n\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer' data-target='computer' data-title='Computer'>\r\n\t\t\tComputer\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os' data-target='computer\/os' data-title='OS'>\r\n\t\t\tOS\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os\/windows' data-target='computer\/os\/windows' data-title='Windows'>\r\n\t\t\tWindows\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n\t\t<a class='XURL content-link' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/n10' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/n10' data-title='10'>\r\n\t\t\t10\t\t<\/a>\r\n\t\t<span class='path-separator'>\\<\/span>\r\n","async":"0","desc":"Pin shortcuts from %Programs%, fix custom .url shortcuts, and how Start menu hash uses Target only.","label":"Start menu","prevArticle":{"id":"computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/personalize","label":"Personalize","url":"\/computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/personalize"},"nextArticle":{"id":"computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/windows_apps","label":"Windows Apps","url":"\/computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/windows_apps"},"languageSwitcher":"<div id='language-switcher'>\n<\/div>\n","content":"<div id='message'>\n\t<p>\n\t\tPlace the shortcut in the <code class='inline'>%Programs%<\/code> directory. It should show up in <strong>Recent<\/strong> on the left side of the Start menu. Pin it.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<h2>Custom .url shortcuts<\/h2>\n\t<p>\n\t\tYou may have to copy the shortcut after placing it, within the same Start menu directory. Delete the original and rename the copy to the original name. It should then show up when searched in the Start menu. Applies to Steam and Epic Games.\n\t<\/p>\n\t<h2>Hash<\/h2>\n\t<p>\n\t\tThe hash does not regard <strong>Start in<\/strong>, only <strong>Target<\/strong>. Target is stripped of leading and lagging spaces.\n\t<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<div id='updated-container'>\r\n\t<div id='updated'>\r\n\t\tUpdated:\r\n\t\t<span id='date'>\r\n\t\t\t2026 Aug 19\t\t<\/span>\r\n\t<\/div>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div class='center' id='content-body-separator'><\/div>\r\n<div id='sub-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n<\/div>\r\n<div id='fb_components'>\r\n\t<div class=\"fb-comments\"\n  data-href=\"https:\/\/ujnotes.com\/computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/start_menu\"\n  data-numposts=\"50\">\n<\/div>\n\t<div class=\"fb-like\"\n  data-href=\"https:\/\/ujnotes.com\/computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/start_menu\"\n  data-layout=\"button\"\n  data-action=\"like\"\n  data-size=\"small\"\n  data-show-faces=\"false\"\n  data-share=\"true\">\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\r\n<div id='nav-list' class='center page-list'>\r\n\t<a id='nav-menu-prev'\r\n\t\t\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/personalize' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/personalize' data-title='Personalize' >\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg' loading='lazy' alt='Navigation - previous page tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div class='arrow'>&#x25C4;<\/div><div>Personalize<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t\t<\/a><a id='nav-menu-next'\r\n\t\t\tclass='XURL item_block_container' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/windows_apps' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/n10\/windows_apps' data-title='Windows Apps' >\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image item_block_image_visible' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg' loading='lazy' alt='Navigation - next page tile'><div class='item_block_text'><div>Windows Apps<\/div><div class='arrow'>&#x25BA;<\/div><\/div>\r\n\t\t<\/a><a id='nav-menu-up' class='XURL item_block_container ' href='\/computer\/os\/windows\/n10' data-target='computer\/os\/windows\/n10' data-title='10'>\r\n\t\t<img class='item_block_image ' loading='lazy' src='\/resource\/placeholder.svg ' alt='Navigation - up level tile'><div class='item_block_t